    Evaluation: 7, Serviceable. Mechanized and documented. Optional response
    interfaces remain abstract. Not peer reviewed.


3 - Intuition
    ---------

    L002 distinguishes two related but unequal positions.

    First, the L001 bottom-goal frame constructs a full negation fixed point:

      ClosureEvaluationFrameForGoal ... Bot
        -> exists chi, ExternalFixedPoint M Gamma chi

      ExternalFixedPoint M Gamma chi
        -> regulator_theory_checked_derivable M Gamma Bot

    Thus the L001 construction marks the collapsing boundary. It does not
    construct the live L002 position.

    The live position retains only the direction `¬chi -> chi`. If `chi` and
    `¬chi` cannot both be checked at that formula, a checked refutation would
    reconstruct `chi` and violate local consistency:

      ExternalMirrorPosition M Gamma chi
        -> MirrorLocallyConsistent M Gamma chi
        -> AsIF M Gamma chi

    Coded recognition accepts exactly when the missing direction
    `chi -> ¬chi` has checked evidence. Acceptance would therefore complete the
    full fixed point, so the same local premise excludes it:

      ExternalMirrorPosition M Gamma chi
        -> MirrorLocallyConsistent M Gamma chi
        -> ~ CodedRecognitionAccepted M Gamma chi

    Global `MirrorConsistent` supplies local consistency at every formula and
    yields the retained compatibility forms of both theorems.

    At finite recursive depth, the same reasoning is pointwise:

      RecursiveMirrorAdequacy M Gamma mirror_step chi
        -> RecursiveMirrorLocallyConsistent M Gamma mirror_step chi
        -> RecursiveMirrorPosition M Gamma mirror_step chi /\
           forall depth,
             ~ CodedRecognitionAccepted M Gamma
                 (recursive_mirror_formula depth mirror_step chi)

    No unbounded formula, semantic fixed point, or infinite execution is
    constructed. The response, recurrence, attribution, and externalization
    layers are separate interfaces built over this finite theorem core.


